# Record what the game plays, for tools/audio_check.py to correlate against
# the disc's own stream.
name: audio
summary: The opening, headless, with every mixed sample written to a WAV file.
frames: 11500
pad: 1600:start,1640:a,1800:start,1840:a,2000:start,2040:a,2200:start,2240:a
pad: 2400:start,2440:a,2600:start,2640:a,2800:start,2840:a,3000:start,3040:a
pad: 3200:start,3240:a
pad: 3600:a@150
env: SOA_WAV=build/opening.wav
env: SOA_NOSOUND=1

shows: the AX mixer and the AI DMA path end to end: the report's [ax] line
shows:   counts mixed frames and voice-frames, [audio] counts DMA blocks and
shows:   the peak sample.
shows: the streamed music, which is the one audio path with a reference:
shows:   python tools/audio_check.py build/opening.wav extracted/sound/m01_L.dsp
shows:   correlates the opening theme at 0.85 on both channels, the battle music
shows:   at 0.52 under the voices mixed over it (FINDINGS "Streamed music,
shows:   checked").

evidence: build/boot_wav.log: 19 scripted events, A every 150 frames out to
evidence:   11400, no [gxr] line (headless, no rendering), and build/opening.wav
evidence:   beside it is what that run wrote.

note: SOA_NOSOUND=1 keeps the run off the machine's sound device, which it
note:   would otherwise wait on; the WAV is written either way. Every saved
note:   report so far says "(no output device)", so no sample from this port has
note:   ever reached a speaker (PLAN E3).
note: The first nine START/A pairs are the standard preamble: START at 1600
note:   dismisses the title, A at 1640 takes New Game, and the eight pairs that
note:   follow walk the first dialogue boxes. From 3600 one A press every 150
note:   frames advances everything after that. Every saved run in build/ that
note:   got past the title begins with exactly these nineteen events.
